<title>JAPAN: Yaohan Japan shares up on restructuring reports.</title>
<headline>Yaohan Japan shares up on restructuring reports.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yaohan Japan Corp rebounded to end up on Monday after media reports said it would freeze plans to open 100 new supermarkets in Japan as a part of its restructuring measures, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares closed four yen up at 470 after early losing 19 yen on heavy turnover of 2.39 million shares.</p>
<p>Company officials were not available for comment on the reports.</p>
<p>However, the company said earlier that it would hold a news conference on its business at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT) at the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
